course: dictionary
lesson: 5904
title: Marcher: a walker in a march
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Context means the words around a word, and they often give clues to its meaning. A marcher is a person who walks in a march. Look at the phrases «protest marchers», «peace marchers» and «thousands of marchers». Who is walking, and why? The clues tell you they are walking together to show something.
explain: Protest and peace are clues that marchers want people to notice what they believe. Parades and bands are clues that marchers walk in step, all moving together. Ask yourself what word would fit, then try your meaning in the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
explain: The same spelling can mean something different in another language. «Défense de marcher sur la pelouse» is French. Défense de means it is forbidden to, and la pelouse is the lawn. So marcher means to walk, and the sign says «Keep off the grass». Check the words around a word to find out which language it belongs to.
fact: A marcher is a person who walks in a march.
fact: Marchers in a protest walk to show what they believe.
fact: Marchers in a parade walk in step, like bands on Remembrance Day or St Patrick's Day.
fact: In history, the Marcher Lords were powerful nobles who ruled the borderlands, «the Marches», between England and Wales.
fact: In French, marcher means to walk, as in «Défense de marcher sur la pelouse».
exercise: What is a marcher? | A person who builds a wall | A person who sells newspapers | *A person who walks in a march | A person who runs in a race
exercise: In «thousands of marchers», what does marcher mean? | To swim across a river | To sing in a choir | To sleep in a tent | *A person walking in a march
exercise: In «Défense de marcher sur la pelouse», what does marcher mean? | *To walk | To swim | To sing | To sleep
test: «Protest marchers» carried signs about fair pay. Why are they marching? | To watch a film | *To show what they believe | To sell ice cream | To find lost keys
test: Which clue tells you the marchers are in a parade? | *They walked in step with the band | They whispered in the library | They hid behind a tree | They ate their lunch quickly
exam: In «Défense de marcher sur la pelouse», which word means walk? | Pelouse | Sur | *Marcher | Défense
